 trigger App2, which can be implemented using Azure Logic Apps or Azure Fun=
ctions with an HTTP trigger. This requires minimal development effort and a=
voids the need for additional infrastructure or messaging layers.</p><p><br=
></p><p><code><strong>Azure Event Grid</strong></code> is <strong>incorrect=
</strong> because it is designed for event-driven architectures involving A=
zure services and requires publishers to be registered within Event Grid. W=
hile powerful, it adds unnecessary complexity for a simple webhook-style in=
teraction between two custom apps.</p><p><br></p><p><code><strong>Azure Ser=
vice Bus</strong></code> is <strong>incorrect</strong> because it is used f=
or reliable messaging between distributed systems, with support for queues =
and topics. It is better suited for complex message workflows with retries,=
 ordering, and dead-lettering. It introduces more development and operation=
al overhead than a straightforward HTTP webhook integration.</p><p><br></p>=
